      },
      "message": "fix(ui): name the platform's command key in shortcut hints\n\nThe ribbon tips, operation-bar hints, machine-cell hover and the\ncleared-toolpath status said Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+N ..., but the keyboard layer\nbinds egui's command modifier, which is Cmd on macOS. One helper\n(shortcut_keys::chord) now builds every command-shortcut hint: Cmd on\nmacOS, Ctrl elsewhere. Ctrl+click pick hints stay Ctrl: those bindings\nread the real Control modifier on every platform.\n\nFixes #1239\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
